landing a role in a superhero movie  comes with more than just a nice  paycheck and a steady work opportunity  afters are now expected to get in  superhuman shape for action roles and  Margot Robbie as Harley Quinn is no  exception here's how she got into havoc  wreaking shape of course Margot Robbie  is fully dedicated to playing Harley  Quinn now but she originally got the  role without even having to convince  anyone she wanted it the actors told MTV  News that the team behind Suicide Squad  approached her with the role offering  her the part without even having to  audition I actually got offered this one  I didn't lose audition which was a real  step up as an actor when you can get  offered things as it turns out the  producers were captivated by Robbie's  performance alongside Will Smith in the  2015 movie focus Smith was already  locked in to play Deadshot and Suicide  Squad wanted to recreate that connection  when they cast their Harley Quinn I  guess they knew that will and I worked  well together so that was a given we  didn't have to do like chemistry roots  or anything like that the studio's  gamble paid off and while the overall  reviews for Suicide Squad were in less  than enthusiastic the dynamic between  Smith and Robbie was a consistent high  point of the film you're my friend to  stay evil doll face Margot Robbie is  already in pretty great shape thanks to  working out four or five times a week  for an hour each session according to  Hollywood personal trainer Andy Hecker  to get in fighting shape for her comic  book movie however she ramped that up to  three hours per day as part of a ballet  based fitness program that Hecker  operates Robbie worked out in three hour  blocks nearly every day for three weeks  while filming Suicide Squad pecker told  People magazine that the focus on  Hartley's body and her skimpy costumes  pushed Robbie to work out that much  harder according to Hecker there's a  scene in Suicide Squad where she changes  clothes in front of a bunch of dudes  so her abs needed to be impeccable and  in those tiny shorts Harley wears her  but was constantly on display the parts  of Robbie's body that were on screen for  most of Suicide Squad became the focus  of her tailored workouts Hecker came up  with an exercise routine that would  transform Robbie from a glamorous  starlet into the tough and acrobatic  Harley Quinn according to hacker Margot  wanted to  lean out and tone up she's already  slender but we wanted to make her a  little stronger to achieve these goals  most of Robby's workout regimen  consisted of non bulking cardio  exercises like ballet jumps as a former  dancer who runs a ballet training  program pecker told people that the  jumps ballet dancers perform are quote  surprisingly the most challenging form  of cardio I have ever come across  but despite the relative difficulty of  the exercises pecker said that Robbie  rarely ever faltered in her commitment  to the routine Hecker compared Robbie to  a machine when she spoke to the Los  Angeles Times the actress's workouts  apparently resembled dance marathons  where other clients of Hecker's would  steadily throw in the towel while Robbie  kept at it relentlessly pecker shared  that other people would try the workout  along with us but she kept going when  other people were dropping off it's so  challenging to keep up that level of  intensity but she powered through it  pecker also ran the actress through a  weightlifting regimen intended to tone  her butt thighs and legs she spoke of  Robbie's workout on a granular level in  the lead-up to suicide squads release  telling publications the exact types of  exercises Robbie went through while  trying to embody Harley Quinn  she said that they went for a lower  number of reps with more weight a focus  on Form and engaging the correct muscle  groups in an interview with The  Hollywood Reporter pecker explained she  had to look sexy and strong we do lower  reps so 20 leg lifts with that ankle  weight on and then take a break to move  on to the other leg to do another 20  making sure her glutes were doing it and  not her hamstrings if that robotic  intensity is making you feel like you'll  never be able to attain a form like  Margot Robbie's don't worry  while Hecker painted a picture of the  actress as an ultra dedicated workhorse  in the gym  Robbie herself revealed that she is far  from disciplined when it comes to her  diet in an interview with Emirates woman  Robbie admitted that she can't handle  calorie cutting diets and that cutting  delicious and fatty foods from her life  makes her miserable I'm not good at  doing moderation I can't just have a  salad every day and a half a glass of  wine every second day I can't do it  Robbie told the publication that our  diet largely consisted of beer fries and  burgers which she burned off in the gym  she added  that she has a rather unhealthy way of  cutting weight quickly if a rule calls  for it saying if I have to get in a  bikini then I'll eat carrot sticks for  three days I'm one extreme or the other  successfully pushing to get a standalone  Harley Quinn movie made meant that  Robbie had to get back into Suicide  Squad shape in which she was able to  perform most of her own stunts  according to Suicide Squad co-producer  Andy Horowitz Margaret doesn't 97% of  her stunts in this movie she embraced  everything we throw at her she makes it  her own and does it better than we could  have ever assumed it was gonna be  however when it came to revisiting  Harley for birds of prey Robbie said  many of the stunts in the new film were  actually too dangerous to take on  there's a lot of really cool stunts in  the birds of prey movie quite a few of  them I couldn't do because they were  just too risky that's not to say that  Robbie slacked off in comparison to her  work for Suicide Squad though in  addition to her regular workouts  Robbie trained to roller-skate ahead of  birds of prey after already learning to  ice-skate for her role in a Tonya photos  of Robbie training and shooting in  rollerskates circulated on comic book  blogs ahead of the movie's release  revealing that prey will be based on a  later version of Harley Quinn modeled  after roller derby players the roller  skating Harley Quinn comes from the new  52 reboot in the DC Universe which  remodeled many characters with a hard  refresh of 52 titles even a newish  character like Quinn was not immune from  the mandate the most recent version of  Quinn has been completely removed from  the Joker as she finally split with the  Clown Prince of Crime for good with her  newfound independence Quinn's  motivations have also shifted where  before most of her actions could be  explained as working for mr. J the newly  single Quinn is considerably less  villainous she's become a sort of anti  heroic vigilante toeing the line between  criminal and superhero while attempting  to hold her home of Coney Island  together the new Quinn is in the mold of  wisecracking weirdos with murky morals  like deadpool and screenwriter Christina  Hudson even cited the Merc with a mouth  when she talked about her early talks  with Margot Robbie around the film  Robbie's dedication to the character is  bound to translate to the big screen  once again as it did in Suicide Squad  and  fitting that birds of praise reviews are  a big improvement over the reaction to  Suicide Squad it's likely that we will  be seeing Robbie as a ripped Harley  Quinn for years to come  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and TV shows are  coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

